VFS: do not walk the dev checkout's out/, .git and thirdparty at startup (perf-3x 2026-10-11).
Applied by tools/build_sdk_from_source.py (SDK_BEHAVIOUR_PATCHES). FABLE2_VFS_SKIP_DEV_DIRS=0
restores the full walk.

Dev sessions mount the repository root as game:\ (--game_data_root). HostPathDevice::Initialize
populated the whole tree recursively (opendir + stat per entry): ~179k entries, 162k of them under
out/ (dev sessions, builds), so the gap between "Guest memory arena mapped" and the GPU Commands
thread grew from 0.6 to 1.1 s as out/ grew (`sample` of a boot: 76% of the main thread in
PopulateEntry). Only top-level children of the device root named out, .git or thirdparty are
skipped: their entry stays. HostPathDevice::ResolvePath's lazy fallback (exact stat per missing
component) now also walks every directory it adds: VirtualFileSystem::OpenFile resolves the
parent directory, then calls the base Entry::GetChild on it, so an unwalked directory made every
open below it fail (first version of this patch: skip intro's game:\out\skipintro\*.bik
reported missing and the intro movies played; bug-patterns row 53).
Other mounts (saves, cache, the playtest/portable game-data roots) have no such directories.

